fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6526120Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6538361Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6641888Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6652092Z ^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6652975Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6654059Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6654577Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6654967Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6656588Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6657212Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6657605Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6658169Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6658376Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6658811Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6659398Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6659956Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6660353Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6660553Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6660835Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6661147Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6661442Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6662214Z    can use Nix.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6662546Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6662777Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6663121Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6663702Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6664309Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6668099Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6668372Z I will:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6668752Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6669428Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6670071Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6670639Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6671159Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6671571Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6671950Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6672459Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6672961Z    /root
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6685427Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6686335Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6697281Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6698049Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6698578Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6699498Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6700209Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6718480Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6729410Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6730312Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6731126Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6731664Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6732259Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.6732528Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
