archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4611827Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4620245Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4621095Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4621690Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4621950Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:40.4622331Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
