creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7280260Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7290814Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7392078Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7405546Z ^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7406522Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7406983Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7407322Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7407621Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7408901Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7409366Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7409644Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7410557Z    if you are ready to continue.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7410848Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7411452Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7412237Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7412671Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7413040Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7413192Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7413352Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7413595Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7413776Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7414124Z    can use Nix.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7414251Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7414340Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7414495Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7414752Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7415175Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7416168Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7416304Z I will:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7416587Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7416778Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7417155Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7417540Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7417919Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7418170Z  - install Nix in /nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7418406Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7418789Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7419154Z    /root
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7431794Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7432587Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7443295Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7443835Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7444332Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7445576Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7446155Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7464388Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7464891Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7475301Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7476106Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7476502Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7476685Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7476887Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7477260Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7477570Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7478004Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7478214Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7478321Z If you would like to
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7478582Z see the output, try like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7478817Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7479046Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7479527Z   $ sh ./install-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:14:38.7479665Z 
